:"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8283&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=491874&INSPECTION_NN=491874","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"478617","date":"2023-10-24","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":2,"repeat":1,"grp":0,"label":"Needs attention","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8283&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=478617&INSPECTION_NN=478617","fetched":true,"findings":[{"item":6,"title":"Proper eating, tasting, drinking, or tobacco use","repeat":false,"comment":"(c) 2-401.11 Employee was chewing gum while working in the kitchen. Gum was discarded at request of inspector.\nEmployees shall eat, including gum/candy, only in designated areas where the contamination of exposed food; clean equipment, utensils, and linens; unwrapped single service and single use articles; or other items needing protection cannot result.","citation":"","citation_text":""},{"item":16,"title":"Food-contact surfaces; cleaned and sanitized","repeat":false,"comment":"(P) 4-501.114 Quat solution in sani-buckets was observed at 0ppm at front service line/prep area and 100ppm in back by 3 part sink. Fresh solutions at 200ppm were provided.\nA quaternary ammonia compound solution shall be used in accordance with the EPA-registered label use instructions and be maintained at the concentration as indicated by the manufacturer's use directions included in the labeling.","citation":"","citation_text":""}]},{"id":"447650","date":"2023-02-23","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":1,"repeat":0,"grp":1,"label":"Minor issues","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8283&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=447650&INSPECTION_NN=447650","fetched":true,"findings":[{"item":16,"title":"Food-contact surfaces; cleaned and sanitized","repeat":false,"comment":"","citation":"4-501.114","citation_text":"4-501.114 Quat solution in the front service line sani-bucket was observed at 100ppm. All other solutions were at 200ppm. Fresh solution was provided at 200ppm. Allow dispenser to run for several seconds and ensure chemical is moving through the suction line prior to filing buckets and 3 part sink. Use test strips to verify concentration.\nA quaternary ammonia compound solution shall be used in accordance with the EPA-registered label use instructions and be maintained at the concentration as indicated by the manufacturer's use directions included in the labeling."},{"item":48,"title":"Warewashing facilities: installed, maintained, & used; test strips","repeat":false,"comment":"","citation":"4-501.15","citation_text":"4-501.15 Rinse gauge of dish machine was reading at 120F after ware washing cycles were completed. Wash gauge was reading at ~164F, and dish temp tester showed the final rinse surface temperature to be at 160F and 162F for consecutive cycles. After five more cycles the rinse gauge read at 140F. Kitchen manager will have maintenance check the machine and call for outside service if maintenance is unable to fix the issue. \nA warewashing machine and its auxiliary components shall be operated in accordance with the machine's data plate and other manufacturer's instructions."}]},{"id":"431656","date":"2022-09-21","visit":"Spot check","type_raw":"Spot Check","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8283&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=431656&INSPECTION_NN=431656","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"431529","date":"2022-09-20","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":1,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"Minor issues","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8283&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=431529&INSPECTION_NN=431529","fetched":true,"findings":[{"item":16,"title":"Food-contact surfaces; cleaned and sanitized","repeat":false,"comment":"The dish machine food contact surface temperature was observed at 154 F. The rinse temperature was observed at approximately 130F, and the wash temperature was observed at approximately 155F. The dish machine must achieve a minimum food-contact surface temperature of 160F. Ensure the dish machine is serviced so that can be achieved. Dishes may still be washed in the dish machine, but dishes must be sanitized in the 3 part sink. The manager stated that dishes will be sanitized in the 3 part sink until the dish machine is sanitizing properly. \n\n4-703.11: After cleaning, FOOD-CONTACT SURFACES shall be SANITIZED in: (A) manual hot water operations. (B) mechanical hot water operations. (C) Chemical manual or mechanical operations. Contact times shall be consistent with those on EPA-registered label use  standard contact time 30 seconds.","citation":"","citation_text":""}]},{"id":"410030","date":"2022-02-23","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8283&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=410030&INSPECTION_NN=410030","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"397594","date":"2021-09-28","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8283&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=397594&INSPECTION_NN=397594","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"384773","date":"2021-04-29","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/Sh